import scene_equipment.dl

to [place website Farm character] {a pointer to website Farm character:character} [with weight] {floating-point number:weight}:
    set motion to character's motion
    set instance to character's object's instance
    set pose to instance's root pose
    set pose's position to motion's position
    set height to 0.022 if character's kind = 0, else 0.012
    set pose's position's y to pose's position's y + (the absolute value of (the sine of motion's phase)) * height * weight
    set pose's rotation's y to motion's yaw
    set pose's scale to a UI scene vector from [0.75,0.75,0.75] if character's kind = 2, else (a UI scene vector from [1.0,1.0,1.0])
    set UI scene root pose in instance to pose

to get [pose website Farm character] {a pointer to website Farm character:character} [at] {floating-point number:time} [over] {floating-point number:seconds} [seconds dragging] {boolean:dragging}:
    if dragging and (character's kind != 0):
        return false
    set motion to character's motion
    set moving to false
    if dragging = false:
        set moving to advance UI scene motion motion by seconds seconds
        place website Farm character character with weight (motion's weight)
    set weight to 0.0 if dragging, else motion's weight
    set instance to character's object's instance
    set count to 4 if character's kind = 1, else 2
    set gain to 0.48 if character's kind = 0, else 0.35
    loop slot from 0 to count:
        set leg to the item at slot in (character's legs)
        set pose to the item at leg in (instance's poses)
        set pose's rotation's x to (the sine of (motion's phase + slot * 3.141592653589793)) * gain * weight
        set UI scene pose of part leg in instance to pose
    if character's kind = 0:
        set arms to pose website Farm arms of character at time with weight weight over (the minimum of 0.08 and seconds) seconds
        set moving to moving or arms
    else if character's kind = 1:
        set pose to the item at (character's tail) in (instance's poses)
        set pose's rotation's z to (the sine of (time * 2.0)) * 0.18
        set UI scene pose of part (character's tail) in instance to pose
    else:
        set pose to the item at (character's head) in (instance's poses)
        set pose's rotation's x to (the maximum of 0.0 and (the sine of (time * 3.0 + character's phase offset))) * 0.45 * (1.0 - weight)
        set UI scene pose of part (character's head) in instance to pose
    return moving or instance's pending
